# T-JEPA: Tabular Joint-Embedding Predictive Architecture

PyTorch replication of **T-JEPA** (ICLR 2025) — a self-supervised learning method for tabular data based on joint-embedding predictive architecture.

> **Paper:** [T-JEPA: Tabular Joint-Embedding Predictive Architecture](https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.05016)  
> T-JEPA learns rich representations from unlabeled tabular features by predicting masked target feature representations from context features using a transformer-based encoder and predictor.

---

## Overview

This repository provides a clean, end-to-end implementation of T-JEPA demonstrated on the **Adult Income** dataset. The pipeline:

1. **Downloads & preprocesses** tabular data (numerical + categorical features)
2. **Pre-trains T-JEPA** in a self-supervised manner (no labels used)
3. **Extracts representations** from the pre-trained context encoder
4. **Trains a downstream MLP classifier** on the frozen T-JEPA representations
5. **Trains a baseline MLP** on raw features for direct comparison
6. **Reports test accuracy** for both approaches

---

## Architecture

| Component | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| **Feature Embedding** | Per-feature linear projection + learned index & type embeddings (numerical vs categorical) |
| **Context Encoder** | Transformer encoder trained by gradient descent |
| **Target Encoder** | EMA (Exponential Moving Average) copy of the context encoder — no gradients |
| **Predictor** | Lightweight transformer that predicts target feature representations from context representations |
| **Masking Strategy** | Random context/target masks with configurable ratios; multiple non-overlapping target masks per sample |

---

## File Structure

```
.
├── data.py          # Data loading, preprocessing, and PyTorch Dataset/DataLoader
├── model.py         # T-JEPA model: FeatureEmbedding, TransformerEncoder, Predictor, TJEPA
├── trainer.py       # Pre-training and downstream training loops
├── downstream.py    # MLP classifiers on top of T-JEPA representations
├── run.py           # End-to-end pipeline script
├── requirements.txt # Python dependencies
└── README.md        # This file
```

