## Usage

### Quick Start

Run the full pipeline with default hyperparameters:

```bash
python run.py
```

### Custom Configuration

```bash
python run.py \
  --epochs-pretrain 100 \
  --epochs-downstream 100 \
  --hidden-dim 128 \
  --num-heads 8 \
  --num-layers 6 \
  --batch-size 512 \
  --lr-pretrain 1e-4 \
  --device cuda
```

### Command-Line Arguments

| Argument | Default | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `--hidden-dim` | 64 | Transformer hidden dimension |
| `--num-heads` | 4 | Number of attention heads |
| `--num-layers` | 4 | Number of transformer encoder layers |
| `--ffn-dim` | 256 | Feed-forward network dimension |
| `--pred-dim` | 32 | Predictor hidden dimension |
| `--epochs-pretrain` | 50 | Number of pre-training epochs |
| `--epochs-downstream` | 50 | Number of downstream training epochs |
| `--batch-size` | 256 | Batch size for training |
| `--lr-pretrain` | 3e-4 | Learning rate for T-JEPA pre-training |
| `--lr-downstream` | 1e-3 | Learning rate for downstream classifier |
| `--ema-decay` | 0.998 | EMA decay rate for target encoder |
| `--device` | cuda (if available) | Device to run on: `cpu` or `cuda` |

---

## Pipeline Steps

The `run.py` script executes the following steps:

```
[1/6] Loading & preprocessing data …
[2/6] Building T-JEPA model …
[3/6] Pre-training T-JEPA for N epochs …
[4/6] Extracting T-JEPA representations …
[5/6] Training downstream MLP on T-JEPA representations …
[6/6] Training baseline sklearn MLP on raw features …
```

At the end, a summary comparing **Baseline MLP** vs **T-JEPA + MLP** test accuracies is printed.

---

## Key Implementation Details

- **Self-Supervised Pre-training:** No labels are used during T-JEPA pre-training. The model learns by predicting masked target feature representations from context features.
- **EMA Target Encoder:** The target encoder is updated via exponential moving average of the context encoder weights, providing stable target representations.
- **Per-Feature Processing:** Each feature has its own projection layer; features are not flattened into a single vector, preserving tabular structure.
- **Categorical Handling:** Categorical features are one-hot encoded before projection.
- **Gradient Clipping:** Max norm of 1.0 is applied during pre-training for stability.
- **Cosine Annealing:** Learning rate schedule used for both pre-training and downstream phases.

---

## Extending to Other Datasets

To use T-JEPA on your own tabular dataset:

1. Replace `load_adult()` in `run.py` with your data loading function
2. Ensure it returns: `(df, target_col, num_cols, cat_cols)`
3. The rest of the pipeline (`build_loaders`, `TJEPA`, training loops) remains unchanged

